00:14:22,933 --> 00:14:24,000
<i> Get up!</i>

252
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:25,267
[BLOWS LAND]

253
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:33,100
[BLOWS LANDING]

254
00:14:33,100 --> 00:14:39,267
- [GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]
- [PEOPLE CLAMORING]

255
00:14:39,267 --> 00:14:40,500
[KICK LANDS]

256
00:14:43,133 --> 00:14:44,133
<i> You bastard!</i>

257
00:14:44,133 --> 00:14:45,100
[GABO PANTING]

258
00:14:45,100 --> 00:14:47,333
<i>I'll never forget
what you did to me.</i>

259
00:14:47,333 --> 00:14:49,933
[PANTING]

260
00:14:49,933 --> 00:14:51,267
<i> I'm leaving your group.</i>

261
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:56,100
[BLOWS LANDING]

262
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:58,100
<i> If I see you here again...</i>

263
00:14:59,333 --> 00:15:01,100
<i> I will kill you!</i>

264
00:15:02,167 --> 00:15:05,133
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GRUNTS]

265
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:10,233
[GABO HUFFS]

266
00:15:10,233 --> 00:15:17,200
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]

267
00:15:26,967 --> 00:15:29,533
[POLICE SIRENS WAILING]

268
00:15:29,533 --> 00:15:30,567
[TIRES SCREECH]

269
00:15:30,567 --> 00:15:35,367
[SIRENS CONTINUE WAILING]

270
00:15:36,233 --> 00:15:37,567
<i> Nobody make a move!</i>

271
00:15:43,267 --> 00:15:44,567
[COP] Hands up!

272
00:15:44,567 --> 00:15:51,533
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]

273
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:54,167
[GUN CLATTERS]

274
00:16:01,200 --> 00:16:08,167
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]

275
00:16:18,367 --> 00:16:20,600
[RAT SQUEAKING]

276
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:26,100
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

277
00:16:26,100 --> 00:16:27,233
[METAL GATE RATTLES]

278
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:30,600
- Stand up!
- What do you want from me?!

279
00:16:31,433 --> 00:16:32,567
What are you
going to do to me?!

280
00:16:33,133 --> 00:16:34,333
What are you
going to do to me?!

281
00:16:35,467 --> 00:16:37,633
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GRUNTING, GROANING]

282
00:16:37,633 --> 00:16:42,600
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

283
00:16:42,633 --> 00:16:43,800
[OFFICER] Now what?!

284
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:44,967
[GABO] What are you
going to do to me?!

285
00:16:44,967 --> 00:16:46,300
Let me go!

286
00:16:46,300 --> 00:16:48,067
- Walk! Just walk!
- [RAT SQUEAKING]

287
00:16:48,067 --> 00:16:49,400
[GABO] What are you
going to do?!

288
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:51,133
Let me go! [GRUNTS]

289
00:16:52,633 --> 00:16:54,133
You're stubborn, huh!

290
00:16:54,500 --> 00:16:55,667
- [BODY THUD]
- [GABO GROANS]

291
00:16:55,667 --> 00:17:02,000
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

292
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:03,133
What are you
going to do to me?!

293
00:17:04,933 --> 00:17:06,267
Come on.

294
00:17:06,267 --> 00:17:08,100
- Stand up!
- Stand up!

295
00:17:09,633 --> 00:17:11,333
- [GRUNTS]
- Let me go!

296
00:17:11,333 --> 00:17:13,167
Come here! [GROANS]

297
00:17:13,167 --> 00:17:15,133
I heard you're tough.

298
00:17:15,167 --> 00:17:16,233
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [GRUNTS]

299
00:17:16,700 --> 00:17:20,667
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GABO GRUNTING]

300
00:17:20,667 --> 00:17:22,100
Fix yourself!

301
00:17:22,100 --> 00:17:23,700
- [GABO EXHALES]
- Go!

302
00:17:23,700 --> 00:17:25,200
- [WATER SPLASHING]
- [GURGLING]

303
00:17:25,200 --> 00:17:26,533
- Don't stop!
- Aah!

304
00:17:26,533 --> 00:17:30,433
- [WATER SPLASHING]
- [GABO GURGLING]

305
00:17:30,433 --> 00:17:32,200
- [GRUNTS]
- [GABO PANTS]

306
00:17:32,200 --> 00:17:33,667
- What?
- One more!

307
00:17:34,367 --> 00:17:40,000
- [WATER SPLASHING]
- [GABO GURGLING]

308
00:17:40,933 --> 00:17:45,700
[GABO PANTING]

309
00:17:45,700 --> 00:17:46,700
What?!

310
00:17:46,700 --> 00:17:48,133
- Oh, okay!
- Go!

311
00:17:48,700 --> 00:17:49,667
[THUD]

312
00:17:50,300 --> 00:17:54,633
[GRUNTING]

313
00:17:57,733 --> 00:17:58,700
You're tough, huh!

314
00:17:58,700 --> 00:18:04,000
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

315
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:06,267
- [ROPE CREAKS]
- [GABO GRUNTS, GROANS]

316
00:18:07,733 --> 00:18:10,167
[BASIN SLIDES]

317
00:18:10,167 --> 00:18:10,900
[RAT SQUEAKS]

318
00:18:10,900 --> 00:18:12,667
- [GRUNTS]
- [WATER SPLASHES]

319
00:18:13,633 --> 00:18:15,700
[GROANING]

320
00:18:16,300 --> 00:18:17,700
Don't fight back!

321
00:18:17,700 --> 00:18:19,000
- [BLOW LANDS]
- Speak up!

322
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:21,733
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

323
00:18:21,767 --> 00:18:22,733
[WATER SPLASHES]

324
00:18:22,733 --> 00:18:24,067
[GROANS]

325
00:18:28,767 --> 00:18:30,300
Whatever you do...

326
00:18:31,267 --> 00:18:32,700
...you can't make me bend!

327
00:18:34,233 --> 00:18:35,367
You're tough.

328
00:18:37,233 --> 00:18:38,200
He's really tough.

329
00:18:38,667 --> 00:18:40,700
[ELECTRIC SPARKS]

330
00:18:40,700 --> 00:18:42,733
Let's see how tough you are.

331
00:18:42,733 --> 00:18:44,733
- Mm-hmm. Let's see.
- [ELECTRIC SPARKING]

332
00:18:52,433 --> 00:18:55,533
[PANTING, GRUNTING]

333
00:18:55,567 --> 00:18:56,567
[ELECTRIC SPARKING]

334
00:19:01,467 --> 00:19:04,067
- [SCREAMING]
- [BUZZING]

335
00:19:05,700 --> 00:19:07,533
[GROANS IN PAIN]

336
00:19:09,800 --> 00:19:13,800
- [SCREAMING]
- [BUZZING]

337
00:19:13,800 --> 00:19:16,767
[SCREAMING]

338
00:19:19,767 --> 00:19:21,733
[GRUNTING]

339
00:19:22,467 --> 00:19:23,733
[BUZZING]

340
00:19:23,733 --> 00:19:25,633
[SCREAMING]

341
00:19:25,633 --> 00:19:27,200
[WATER SPLASHING]

342
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:29,500
[BUZZING CONTINUES]

343
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:33,833
[GROANING]

344
00:19:33,833 --> 00:19:39,800
[ELECTRIC BUZZING]

345
00:19:39,800 --> 00:19:44,133
[GABO'S SCREAMS ECHOING]

346
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:54,567
- Herode.
- Sir.

347
00:19:54,567 --> 00:19:56,633
[GABO GROANING]

348
00:19:56,633 --> 00:20:02,067
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

349
00:20:02,100 --> 00:20:03,867
Let's see how tough you are!

350
00:20:03,867 --> 00:20:09,633
[SCREAMING]

351
00:20:12,167 --> 00:20:17,067
- [SCREAMING CONTINUES]
- [ROPE TWISTING]

352
00:20:19,600 --> 00:20:22,600
- [THWACKS]
- [GABO GRUNTS]

353
00:20:22,600 --> 00:20:23,867
- [KICK LANDS]
- [GRUNTS]

354
00:20:23,867 --> 00:20:27,233
[GUARDS GRUNTING]

355
00:20:28,833 --> 00:20:31,867
- [KICK LANDS]
- [BODY THUDS]

356
00:20:31,867 --> 00:20:39,133
[KICKS LANDING]

357
00:20:39,167 --> 00:20:41,367
- [BODY THUDS]
- [WOOD CLATTERS]

358
00:20:41,367 --> 00:20:45,233
[KICKS LANDING]

359
00:20:45,233 --> 00:20:47,867
- [BODY THUDS]
- [WATER SPLASHES]

360
00:20:49,167 --> 00:20:51,300
- [THUD]
- [GRUNTS]

361
00:20:51,300 --> 00:20:57,233
- [KICKS, BLOWS LANDING]
- [GUARDS GRUNTING]

362
00:20:57,233 --> 00:20:59,267
[BLOW LANDS]

363
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:03,900
- [KICK LANDS]
- [BODY THUDS]

364
00:21:03,900 --> 00:21:07,733
[KICKS LANDING]

365
00:21:07,733 --> 00:21:09,200
[WATER SPLASHES]

366
00:21:09,733 --> 00:21:13,200
[KICKS LANDING]

367
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:17,367
[BLOW, KICKS LAND]

368
00:21:18,933 --> 00:21:25,600
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

369
00:21:25,600 --> 00:21:27,700
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

370
00:21:31,533 --> 00:21:32,567
[KEYS JANGLING]

371
00:21:32,567 --> 00:21:36,633
- Get him in there.
- Hey, get up! Wake up!

372
00:21:38,200 --> 00:21:39,367
Wake up.

373
00:21:39,367 --> 00:21:40,333
Oh, no!

374
00:21:41,767 --> 00:21:43,767
I got him.

375
00:21:43,767 --> 00:21:46,833
[GABO GRUNTING WEAKLY]

376
00:21:50,400 --> 00:21:51,533
Ow!

377
00:21:51,533 --> 00:21:53,367
[MACARAIG] Hey! Listen up!

378
00:21:54,367 --> 00:21:57,733
Anyone who stirs up trouble

379
00:21:57,733 --> 00:21:59,267
will answer to me.

380
00:22:00,533 --> 00:22:03,267
Hey, Grandpa!

381
00:22:03,267 --> 00:22:07,267
Tell him to behave
if he still wants to live!

382
00:22:09,467 --> 00:22:12,933
[OMENG] Go back to sleep!
Go!

383
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:29,767
Drop the brave act, Gabo.

384
00:22:30,800 --> 00:22:33,300
You won't win
against them.

385
00:22:35,667 --> 00:22:39,400
What you should do
is get out of here.

386
00:22:40,500 --> 00:22:42,567
Before they kill you.

387
00:22:42,567 --> 00:22:48,300
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

388
00:22:48,300 --> 00:22:50,967
Gabo, you should
break out tonight.

389
00:22:52,033 --> 00:22:53,767
Gabo.

390
00:22:56,867 --> 00:23:01,333
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

391
00:23:01,333 --> 00:23:03,500
Gabo, this is the key.

392
00:23:03,500 --> 00:23:05,800
When everyone is asleep

393
00:23:05,800 --> 00:23:10,967
head for the exit
and escape.

394
00:23:10,967 --> 00:23:14,300
You won't make it
to sunrise if you don't.

395
00:23:16,700 --> 00:23:23,733
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

396
00:23:33,300 --> 00:23:35,900
[CRICKETS CHIRPING]

397
00:23:35,900 --> 00:23:42,867
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

398
00:23:58,700 --> 00:24:05,733
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

399
00:24:16,900 --> 00:24:21,433
[MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

400
00:24:21,433 --> 00:24:22,900
[LOCK CLINKING]

401
00:24:27,867 --> 00:24:31,433
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

402
00:24:31,467 --> 00:24:32,900
[DOOR CREAKS FAINTLY]

403
00:24:38,467 --> 00:24:45,433
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

404
00:25:00,867 --> 00:25:07,833
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

405
00:25:22,967 --> 00:25:29,933
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

406
00:25:42,533 --> 00:25:49,500
[TENSE MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

407
00:26:03,500 --> 00:26:04,933
- [SIREN BLARING]
- Gabo!

408
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:07,400
Where are you going?

409
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:14,000
[SIREN BLARING]

410
00:26:14,033 --> 00:26:15,933
[TENSE MUSIC SWELLS]

411
00:26:24,733 --> 00:26:27,567
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

412
00:26:27,567 --> 00:26:29,800
- [FLESH SQUELCHING]
- [GUNSHOTS]

413
00:26:35,867 --> 00:26:39,600
[BODY THUDS]

414
00:26:44,600 --> 00:26:51,633
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

415
00:27:07,033 --> 00:27:14,000
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]

416
00:27:14,667 --> 00:27:18,600
[SIREN BLARING DISTANTLY]

417
00:27:18,633 --> 00:27:25,600
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]

418
00:27:39,800 --> 00:27:41,700
I'm not breaking out.

419
00:27:41,700 --> 00:27:43,700
I'm going to fight...

420
00:27:45,633 --> 00:27:47,067
for the truth.

421
00:28:05,833 --> 00:28:07,733
[DOOR SQUEAKS OPEN]

422
00:28:10,833 --> 00:28:11,800
Gabo.

423
00:28:12,333 --> 00:28:13,300
Have a seat.

424
00:28:15,800 --> 00:28:17,133
Why did you call me in?

425
00:28:18,600 --> 00:28:19,767
Good news.

426
00:28:20,067 --> 00:28:22,533
We'll have one less
troublemaker in here.

427
00:28:23,933 --> 00:28:25,600
You're free to go.

428
00:28:30,867 --> 00:28:31,900
[FOLDER SHUFFLES]

429
00:28:34,867 --> 00:28:37,633
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

430
00:28:37,633 --> 00:28:39,167
We're just waiting
for your release order.

431
00:28:44,867 --> 00:28:47,700
Everyone! Gabo is free!

432
00:28:47,700 --> 00:28:49,000
[PRISONERS TALKING INDISTINCTLY]

433
00:28:49,000 --> 00:28:52,300
- Gabo's a free man!
- Take care outside, man.

434
00:28:52,300 --> 00:28:53,367
Be nice in here.

435
00:28:53,367 --> 00:28:55,667
Sure thing!

436
00:28:55,700 --> 00:28:57,000
- Take care, man.
- Hey!

437
00:28:57,000 --> 00:28:58,233
Don't forget about us
when you're out.

438
00:28:58,233 --> 00:28:59,900
I'll be going now.

439
00:28:59,900 --> 00:29:01,667
- Take care.
- Bye, Gabo!

440
00:29:03,733 --> 00:29:06,367
Mister Omeng, Mister Tomas.

441
00:29:06,367 --> 00:29:07,833
I'll be going now.

442
00:29:08,900 --> 00:29:09,967
Take care.

443
00:29:10,733 --> 00:29:11,767
Thank you.

444
00:29:12,700 --> 00:29:13,733
Goodbye.

445
00:29:13,733 --> 00:29:16,233
Oh! Uh, Gabo, wait.

446
00:29:16,233 --> 00:29:19,867
Take this. It's some savings
from the group.

447
00:29:19,867 --> 00:29:21,300
- Take it.
- No, I'm good.

448
00:29:21,300 --> 00:29:23,733
Come on.
It'll help you start again.

449
00:29:23,733 --> 00:29:25,400
- It's okay.
- Thank you.

450
00:29:25,400 --> 00:29:28,733
Gabo, can you also
check on my parole?

451
00:29:28,767 --> 00:29:31,933
Come on now!
What does he know about that?

452
00:29:31,933 --> 00:29:35,000
Well, he doesn't know
about his parole, either.

453
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:36,900
- Who knows?
- Oh, you.

454
00:29:36,900 --> 00:29:38,867
[OMENG]
Just let the kid go out.

455
00:29:38,867 --> 00:29:41,067
I know, I know, but...

456
00:29:41,767 --> 00:29:42,733
Tatang...

457
00:29:43,767 --> 00:29:44,900
I'm going out today.

458
00:29:45,733 --> 00:29:48,333
Oh, it must be nice to be out.

459
00:29:48,333 --> 00:29:49,933
Don't worry, Tatang.

460
00:29:49,933 --> 00:29:52,000
I'm sure
you'll get your day, too.

461
00:29:52,000 --> 00:29:53,867
I'll meet you outside, by then.

462
00:29:54,700 --> 00:29:57,000
I think I'm gonna die in here

463
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:58,867
because of my sentence.

464
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:02,067
Tatang, don't say that.

465
00:30:02,467 --> 00:30:04,000
You'll get out too.

466
00:30:04,433 --> 00:30:06,200
I hope, Gabo,

467
00:30:06,700 --> 00:30:09,900
you don't waste this opportunity

468
00:30:09,900 --> 00:30:11,300
in your life.

469
00:30:11,300 --> 00:30:15,700
Do your best to not
come back here.

470
00:30:18,233 --> 00:30:19,400
Don't worry.

471
00:30:20,233 --> 00:30:21,700
I promise.

472
00:30:22,300 --> 00:30:23,767
I'm never going back here.

473
00:30:24,733 --> 00:30:27,767
I hope, in your new journey,

474
00:30:27,767 --> 00:30:31,700
you will use your fiery heart

475
00:30:32,233 --> 00:30:33,733
for the good.

476
00:30:33,733 --> 00:30:35,700
I'll keep that in mind,
Tatang.

477
00:30:36,167 --> 00:30:37,900
Mister Omeng, Mister Tomas.

478
00:30:37,900 --> 00:30:39,033
[OMENG] Take care, Gabo.

479
00:30:40,767 --> 00:30:42,767
- Hey, Gabo!
- Hey, it's Gabo!

480
00:30:42,767 --> 00:30:43,933
Gabo is going out!

481
00:30:43,933 --> 00:30:45,767
Gabo, take care!

482
00:30:45,767 --> 00:30:47,167
Take care outside, Gabo!

483
00:30:47,167 --> 00:30:48,733
Take care in here.

484
00:30:49,333 --> 00:30:56,333
[HOPEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

485
00:30:56,333 --> 00:30:59,133
[PRISONERS CHEERING]

486
00:31:11,833 --> 00:31:18,767
[HOPEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

487
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:31,600
[GATE SQUEAKS CLOSE]

488
00:31:32,500 --> 00:31:39,467
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

489
00:31:52,067 --> 00:31:53,333
[BUS CONDUCTOR] Alright, now.

490
00:31:53,333 --> 00:31:55,000
For those who haven't paid up,
bring it in.

491
00:31:55,000 --> 00:31:56,167
Who doesn't have a ticket yet?

492
00:31:56,167 --> 00:31:58,167
- [VENDOR] Peanuts here!
- Come on.

493
00:32:00,833 --> 00:32:02,033
[BUS CONDUCTOR] Wait up!

494
00:32:05,167 --> 00:32:06,700
Come on in!

495
00:32:07,000 --> 00:32:08,667
Who doesn't have ticket yet?

496
00:32:08,667 --> 00:32:09,800
Come on, pay up.

497
00:32:11,300 --> 00:32:18,200
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

498
00:32:22,167 --> 00:32:24,167
Your fare, please.

499
00:32:26,933 --> 00:32:29,033
- Where are you headed?
<i> - Ginintuang Lupa.</i>

500
00:32:29,033 --> 00:32:30,167
<i> Ginintuang Lupa.</i>

501
00:32:33,867 --> 00:32:36,000
[COINS JINGLE]

502
00:32:39,067 --> 00:32:41,033
Who else doesn't have a ticket?

503
00:32:42,367 --> 00:32:43,533
How about you?

504
00:32:45,700 --> 00:32:52,667
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

505
00:32:57,100 --> 00:32:58,867
[GABO] Now that I'm free,

506
00:33:00,200 --> 00:33:02,100
<i> I promise myself.</i>

507
00:33:03,600 --> 00:33:05,667
<i> I'm going to change my ways</i>

508
00:33:06,233 --> 00:33:08,367
<i>and give my life
some direction.</i>

509
00:33:10,233 --> 00:33:13,333
<i>I'm not going to let us
be poor forever,</i>

510
00:33:14,767 --> 00:33:16,700
<i> suffering for eternity.</i>

511
00:33:20,933 --> 00:33:22,200
<i> I will do anything</i>

512
00:33:23,667 --> 00:33:25,367
<i> to get my life in order.</i>

513
00:33:26,633 --> 00:33:28,600
<i> I will help my family</i>

514
00:33:29,133 --> 00:33:30,900
<i> and my neighbors.</i>

515
00:33:32,267 --> 00:33:34,967
[YOUNG GABO] How long
are we going to stay here?

516
00:33:37,233 --> 00:33:39,633
[YOUNG RUDY]
<i> Do you miss our old house?</i>

517
00:33:45,100 --> 00:33:46,800
<i> I miss Mommy.</i>

518
00:33:48,067 --> 00:33:54,933
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

519
00:34:05,767 --> 00:34:06,833
<i> Son...</i>

520
00:34:08,833 --> 00:34:11,067
<i>We're not going back
to our old life.</i>

521
00:34:13,267 --> 00:34:15,333
We can't be with Mommy anymore.

522
00:34:17,833 --> 00:34:19,067
<i> But don't worry.</i>

523
00:34:21,200 --> 00:34:24,300
<i>We won't be
at rock bottom forever.</i>

524
00:34:25,800 --> 00:34:27,000
<i> The earth is round, son.</i>

525
00:34:27,967 --> 00:34:29,767
Our fate will change eventually.

526
00:34:31,200 --> 00:34:32,333
<i> Do you understand?</i>

527
00:34:33,700 --> 00:34:34,967
<i> Yes.</i>

528
00:34:36,067 --> 00:34:37,867
<i>Come here. I'm going
to give you something.</i>

529
00:34:45,467 --> 00:34:47,767
<i> This coin gave me luck.</i>

530
00:34:48,900 --> 00:34:50,433
<i> It changed my life.</i>

531
00:34:52,733 --> 00:34:59,667
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

532
00:35:06,433 --> 00:35:08,367
<i> That will give you luck, too.</i>

533
00:35:24,833 --> 00:35:27,233
[GABO]<i> I will not waste
</i> this opportunity.

534
00:35:29,333 --> 00:35:32,067
<i>This time, I'll change
my family's destiny.</i>

535
00:35:34,067 --> 00:35:35,467
<i> We won't be...</i>

536
00:35:37,400 --> 00:35:39,167
<i> at rock bottom forever.</i>

537
00:35:41,367 --> 00:35:48,333
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

538
00:36:05,767 --> 00:36:10,400
- [HORNS HONKING]
- [SIRENS WAILING]

539
00:36:10,433 --> 00:36:16,500
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

540
00:36:16,500 --> 00:36:21,867
[BLOWS LANDING]

541
00:36:29,833 --> 00:36:36,467
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

542
00:36:52,200 --> 00:36:59,133
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

543
00:37:13,167 --> 00:37:14,333
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

544
00:37:14,967 --> 00:37:16,467
I hope today turns out well.

545
00:37:16,500 --> 00:37:18,000
I'm wearing your watch,
after all.

546
00:37:20,467 --> 00:37:21,867
I miss you, RJ.

547
00:37:21,867 --> 00:37:27,933
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

548
00:37:29,133 --> 00:37:30,667
[MAX] Good morning, sis!

549
00:37:30,667 --> 00:37:32,233
- Good morning, Max.
- Come here.

550
00:37:32,233 --> 00:37:33,600
Mmm, my baby girl.

551
00:37:34,400 --> 00:37:35,433
Hm?

552
00:37:36,533 --> 00:37:38,400
[MAX SIGHS]

553
00:37:38,400 --> 00:37:39,500
Is everything okay?

554
00:37:40,167 --> 00:37:42,067
Thinking about RJ again?

555
00:37:42,067 --> 00:37:43,367
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

556
00:37:43,367 --> 00:37:45,633
Not a day goes by
that I don't think about him.

557
00:37:45,633 --> 00:37:47,467
We all miss him.

558
00:37:48,633 --> 00:37:52,000
Please stop blaming yourself
for what happened.

559
00:37:52,033 --> 00:37:54,100
It wasn't your fault, okay?

560
00:37:54,100 --> 00:37:56,000
If you ever need someone
to talk to,

561
00:37:57,100 --> 00:37:58,200
I'm here.

562
00:37:59,000 --> 00:38:01,000
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY] I know.

563
00:38:01,900 --> 00:38:04,267
How's Dad?

564
00:38:04,267 --> 00:38:05,533
Dad?

565
00:38:08,033 --> 00:38:09,500
He's in a good mood today.

566
00:38:09,500 --> 00:38:11,933
Don't worry about him.

567
00:38:11,933 --> 00:38:14,267
I know things will
get better soon.

568
00:38:14,267 --> 00:38:16,433
So cheer up. Hmm? Hmm?

569
00:38:16,433 --> 00:38:19,033
If you need anything,
I'm just here.

570
00:38:19,033 --> 00:38:20,667
I just need to grab something
from my room.

571
00:38:20,667 --> 00:38:22,900
I'll see you downstairs. Okay?

572
00:38:22,900 --> 00:38:24,267
- See you.
- Mwah!

573
00:38:24,300 --> 00:38:30,600
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

574
00:38:31,533 --> 00:38:32,633
[RICARDO] I'm telling you,

575
00:38:32,633 --> 00:38:35,267
solar power is
a great investment,

576
00:38:35,267 --> 00:38:38,633
especially now that electricity
prices keep going up.

577
00:38:38,633 --> 00:38:41,533
Since we've been saving money
on electricity,

578
00:38:41,533 --> 00:38:45,567
I think it's about time
we buy an electric car.

579
00:38:45,567 --> 00:38:48,233
Gas is so expensive these days.

580
00:38:48,233 --> 00:38:49,367
Oh, ma'am!

581
00:38:49,367 --> 00:38:51,233
A new car would suit you
perfectly

582
00:38:51,233 --> 00:38:53,100
because you're so fresh.

583
00:38:53,100 --> 00:38:54,700
- [LAUGHS]
- What about me?

584
00:38:54,700 --> 00:38:57,400
Of course, sir.
You're also fresh!

585
00:38:57,433 --> 00:38:59,100
[LAUGHING]

586
00:38:59,100 --> 00:39:00,667
Good morning, Mom, Dad.

587
00:39:00,667 --> 00:39:01,933
Oh!

588
00:39:02,733 --> 00:39:06,267
My beautiful daughter.
Mm. [CHUCKLES]

589
00:39:06,267 --> 00:39:08,000
Twinkle, can I have
some coffee, please?

590
00:39:08,000 --> 00:39:08,967
[TWINKLE] Oh, right.

591
00:39:08,967 --> 00:39:11,233
I'll do it. Thank you.

592
00:39:16,333 --> 00:39:17,500
- [RICARDO] Twinkle!
- Sir?

593
00:39:17,500 --> 00:39:19,433
I'll just have water.
Thank you.

594
00:39:19,433 --> 00:39:23,233
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

595
00:39:23,233 --> 00:39:24,200
Uh...

596
00:39:25,067 --> 00:39:27,600
Come on, join us for breakfast.

597
00:39:27,600 --> 00:39:29,433
[MAX] I'm late! I'm late!
I'm late! I'm late!

598
00:39:29,467 --> 00:39:31,133
- Oh.
- [MAX] I got to go.

599
00:39:31,133 --> 00:39:32,633
- I'm running late.
- Oh.

600
00:39:32,633 --> 00:39:35,433
- Dad, I got to go.
- Oh, wait.

601
00:39:35,433 --> 00:39:37,333
- Why?
- Hon, you have to hear this.

602
00:39:37,333 --> 00:39:41,167
Did you know Captain Umali,
her coworker, called me

603
00:39:41,167 --> 00:39:44,600
and commended her
for their buy-bust operation!

604
00:39:44,600 --> 00:39:46,133
Well done, dear.

605
00:39:46,633 --> 00:39:47,767
Good job.

606
00:39:47,767 --> 00:39:49,267
Max, remember...

607
00:39:50,267 --> 00:39:52,433
I have high expectations
for you.

608
00:39:52,800 --> 00:39:55,467
Remember, you're
carrying the surname Jacinto.

609
00:39:59,200 --> 00:40:00,167
Copy, sir.

610
00:40:01,133 --> 00:40:02,133
Carry on.

611
00:40:02,133 --> 00:40:04,000
I got to go. Sis.

612
00:40:05,667 --> 00:40:06,700
Bye.

613
00:40:08,667 --> 00:40:10,600
Oh, how about you, Sam?

614
00:40:11,467 --> 00:40:14,300
How's work at the NCIA?

615
00:40:15,200 --> 00:40:16,533
We're doing alright.

616
00:40:16,533 --> 00:40:19,167
We've just arrested
the Zaragoza syndicate.

617
00:40:19,167 --> 00:40:21,833
They're the ones behind
the bank heists in Manila.

618
00:40:21,833 --> 00:40:23,167
[ISOBEL] Wow!

619
00:40:23,167 --> 00:40:25,500
I heard about that.

620
00:40:25,500 --> 00:40:27,133
And that's very good.

621
00:40:27,133 --> 00:40:29,533
That's one less group
of criminals out there.

622
00:40:29,533 --> 00:40:30,833
Right, hon?

623
00:40:30,833 --> 00:40:32,633
As it should be. Good.

624
00:40:35,700 --> 00:40:37,333
[ISOBEL SIGHS]

625
00:40:37,600 --> 00:40:40,267
- I'd better get going too.
- Wait, you haven't eaten yet.

626
00:40:40,267 --> 00:40:41,667
Oh, it's alright.

627
00:40:41,667 --> 00:40:44,200
- [ISOBEL] Wait. Twinkle!
- [TWINKLE] Yes, ma'am?

628
00:40:44,200 --> 00:40:47,067
- Pack some food for her.
- Okay, ma'am.

629
00:40:51,533 --> 00:40:52,733
[TOTO] Oh, ma'am!

630
00:40:52,733 --> 00:40:54,533
Got her running like a dream!

631
00:40:54,533 --> 00:40:56,533
- Thank you.
- [TOTO CHUCKLES]

632
00:40:56,533 --> 00:40:57,800
[TWINKLE] Ma'am!

633
00:41:00,067 --> 00:41:02,700
Ma'am, Madam Isabel
said you should bring this.

634
00:41:02,700 --> 00:41:03,667
Thank you.

635
00:41:04,400 --> 00:41:06,700
Hey, Sam, eat healthy, okay?

636
00:41:08,533 --> 00:41:10,067
And, um...

637
00:41:11,400 --> 00:41:13,400
And try to be patient
with your dad.

638
00:41:16,233 --> 00:41:17,667
I understand where
Dad's coming from.

639
00:41:19,400 --> 00:41:21,433
Take care. I love you.

640
00:41:22,600 --> 00:41:23,533
Mm.

641
00:41:24,433 --> 00:41:25,567
I love you.

642
00:41:25,567 --> 00:41:26,600
Okay.

643
00:41:26,600 --> 00:41:29,267
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

644
00:41:29,267 --> 00:41:30,267
[ISOBEL] Bye.

645
00:41:31,700 --> 00:41:32,667
Bye!

646
00:41:34,233 --> 00:41:35,767
[ENGINE STARTING]

647
00:41:37,567 --> 00:41:38,533
Hey.

648
00:41:39,100 --> 00:41:40,233
Where's my food?

649
00:41:41,400 --> 00:41:43,633
[TOTO] Give me some food too.

650
00:41:43,667 --> 00:41:44,733
[TWINKLE] Dream on!

651
00:41:47,500 --> 00:41:49,600
She's making my heart flutter!

652
00:41:49,600 --> 00:41:56,467
[BRIGHT MUSIC CONTINUES]

653
00:42:15,933 --> 00:42:17,567
[HORN HONKING]

654
00:42:18,167 --> 00:42:21,567
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [PASSENGERS SCREAMING]

655
00:42:23,367 --> 00:42:25,367
[TIRES SCREECHING]

656
00:42:25,367 --> 00:42:26,533
[PASSENGERS SCREAM]

657
00:42:26,533 --> 00:42:28,800
Hey, Mister!
You're driving too fast!

658
00:42:28,800 --> 00:42:30,800
You're going to kill us
at this rate!

659
00:42:32,800 --> 00:42:34,667
Just hold on tight!

660
00:42:34,667 --> 00:42:36,867
I'm sorry, but we're in a hurry.

661
00:42:36,867 --> 00:42:38,633
We need to pick up
more passengers.

662
00:42:38,633 --> 00:42:40,433
You know how high
gas prices are.

663
00:42:40,433 --> 00:42:41,800
We need to earn money.

664
00:42:41,800 --> 00:42:43,633
[HORN HONKING]

665
00:42:47,533 --> 00:42:52,200
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

666
00:42:52,233 --> 00:42:54,333
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [PASSENGERS SCREAMING]

667
00:42:54,333 --> 00:42:55,500
[CLAMORING]

668
00:42:55,500 --> 00:42:57,300
My goodness, I'm getting off!

669
00:42:57,300 --> 00:42:58,567
You drive so recklessly!

670
00:42:58,567 --> 00:43:00,667
We're all going to die
at this rate!

671
00:43:01,533 --> 00:43:02,700
My goodness!

672
00:43:02,700 --> 00:43:07,600
- [UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]

673
00:43:10,233 --> 00:43:11,533
Keep walking.

674
00:43:11,533 --> 00:43:13,333
There are vacant seats
at the back.

675
00:43:24,833 --> 00:43:26,033
[BUS CONDUCTOR]
There are some seats left.

676
00:43:26,033 --> 00:43:27,367
[ENGINE REVVING]

677
00:43:27,367 --> 00:43:29,900
[BUS CONDUCTOR]
Your fare, please.

678
00:43:29,900 --> 00:43:31,533
Where are you getting off,
mister?

679
00:43:31,533 --> 00:43:32,567
Tondo.

680
00:43:32,567 --> 00:43:38,833
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

681
00:43:43,900 --> 00:43:46,900
- [HORN HONKING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

682
00:43:46,900 --> 00:43:48,233
[PASSENGER] Jeez, mister.

683
00:43:48,233 --> 00:43:53,633
[ENGINE REVVING]

684
00:43:56,733 --> 00:44:02,267
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

685
00:44:04,467 --> 00:44:05,733
Seriously, Noel?!

686
00:44:06,300 --> 00:44:07,300
What happened to it?

687
00:44:07,300 --> 00:44:08,767
I don't know what's wrong
with it, madam.

688
00:44:08,767 --> 00:44:10,567
You never know anything!

689
00:44:10,567 --> 00:44:11,700
Hey!

690
00:44:12,100 --> 00:44:13,567
The car I told you to book,
where is it?

691
00:44:13,567 --> 00:44:14,633
The phone ran out of juice.

692
00:44:14,633 --> 00:44:16,033
Where's the power bank?

693
00:44:16,267 --> 00:44:18,400
Oh no.
I forgot to bring it, madam.

694
00:44:18,733 --> 00:44:19,733
[GROWLS]

695
00:44:19,733 --> 00:44:21,200
So, what do we do now?

696
00:44:21,200 --> 00:44:22,567
I have an important meeting!

697
00:44:23,800 --> 00:44:25,367
- [HORN HONKING]
- [VEHICLE APPROACHING]

698
00:44:25,367 --> 00:44:28,067
Oh, madam, why don't
we just take the bus?

699
00:44:28,067 --> 00:44:29,067
What?!

700
00:44:29,800 --> 00:44:30,867
We have no choice!

701
00:44:30,900 --> 00:44:33,100
- [HORN HONKING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

702
00:44:33,100 --> 00:44:34,333
[PASSENGERS EXCLAIM]

703
00:44:34,333 --> 00:44:35,667
- Let's go, please.
- Fine!

704
00:44:35,667 --> 00:44:37,433
Come on, madam,
let's hop on.

705
00:44:37,433 --> 00:44:39,833
[ENGINE RUMBLING]

706
00:44:39,833 --> 00:44:41,833
Noel is unbelievable.

707
00:44:41,833 --> 00:44:44,133
Just when I'm in a rush
for a meeting,

708
00:44:44,133 --> 00:44:45,433
that's when the car
breaks down.

709
00:44:45,433 --> 00:44:47,633
Because he never checks it!
And you, you're irritating too!

710
00:44:47,633 --> 00:44:48,833
- Madam--
- Don't you know?

711
00:44:48,833 --> 00:44:51,333
The client is about to pay
the down payment

712
00:44:51,333 --> 00:44:52,567
for the condo!

713
00:44:52,567 --> 00:44:55,467
If I don't make it, you're both
going to be in trouble!

714
00:44:55,467 --> 00:44:56,333
Hold on, hold on.

715
00:44:56,333 --> 00:44:57,833
I want to sit there.
Make her leave.

716
00:44:57,833 --> 00:44:59,667
Miss, maybe you could sit
at the back.

717
00:44:59,667 --> 00:45:01,800
[WOMAN] Why? I was here first!

718
00:45:01,800 --> 00:45:03,667
- She should sit there!
- Miss?

719
00:45:03,700 --> 00:45:05,600
It's okay. There's still a
vacant sit here. Come on.

720
00:45:05,600 --> 00:45:07,300
- Please, miss.
- Oh, seriously?!

721
00:45:07,300 --> 00:45:08,333
What a pain!

722
00:45:08,333 --> 00:45:10,200
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

723
00:45:10,200 --> 00:45:11,267
Put some alcohol on it!

724
00:45:11,267 --> 00:45:12,333
[BOTTLE SPRAYING]

725
00:45:12,333 --> 00:45:14,533
Hurry! Come on, faster!

726
00:45:14,533 --> 00:45:16,267
Such a slowpoke!

727
00:45:16,267 --> 00:45:17,833
- Now, sit there! Come on!
- Yes, ma'am.

728
00:45:21,133 --> 00:45:22,467
Looks like we'll make a
killing with her.

729
00:45:22,800 --> 00:45:24,233
She seems loaded.

730
00:45:25,467 --> 00:45:28,167
[HORN HONKING]

731
00:45:28,167 --> 00:45:29,700
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

732
00:45:29,700 --> 00:45:31,733
Fan me! I'm feeling hot!

733
00:45:40,533 --> 00:45:41,733
Alright, everyone.

734
00:45:41,733 --> 00:45:42,733
This is a holdup!

735
00:45:42,733 --> 00:45:44,633
[PASSENGERS SCREAMING IN FEAR]

736
00:45:44,633 --> 00:45:46,400
Give me your bag! Now!

737
00:45:46,400 --> 00:45:47,467
- Do it!
- Keep driving!

738
00:45:47,467 --> 00:45:54,533
- [OVERLAPPING SHOUTING]
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

739
00:45:55,167 --> 00:45:56,200
Just keep driving!

740
00:45:56,567 --> 00:45:58,700
[ENGINE ROARING]

741
00:46:01,800 --> 00:46:03,700
- [WINDOW SHATTERS]
- [HORN HONKING]

742
00:46:06,400 --> 00:46:08,900
[TIRES SCREECHING]

743
00:46:08,900 --> 00:46:12,167
- Hand over your bag!
- [WOMAN] Please, no!

744
00:46:12,200 --> 00:46:14,233
Talk about bad luck, huh?

745
00:46:16,833 --> 00:46:17,833
- [BONES CRACK]
- [WHIMPERS]

746
00:46:17,833 --> 00:46:20,700
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GROANING]

747
00:46:20,700 --> 00:46:21,700
Don't stop!

748
00:46:21,700 --> 00:46:24,333
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

749
00:46:24,333 --> 00:46:25,333
[GEAR STICK CLICKS]

750
00:46:25,333 --> 00:46:28,867
[HORNS HONKING]

751
00:46:29,867 --> 00:46:30,867
- [KICK LANDS]
- [GROANS]

752
00:46:30,867 --> 00:46:31,833
[WINDOW SHATTERS]

753
00:46:32,733 --> 00:46:33,867
Gabo!

754
00:46:34,567 --> 00:46:36,267
So, you're out now.

755
00:46:36,267 --> 00:46:38,933
Who would've thought
we'd meet here?

756
00:46:38,933 --> 00:46:40,567
Damn you, Boy Topak!

757
00:46:40,867 --> 00:46:43,333
Your crew with Django
is ruthless.

758
00:46:43,967 --> 00:46:45,833
You'll even go after cold rice.

759
00:46:46,867 --> 00:46:49,367
Life is so hard these days,

760
00:46:49,567 --> 00:46:51,433
I'd even eat burnt rice.

761
00:46:53,867 --> 00:46:55,167
- [LOUD THWACK]
- [CRIES]

